From 121fd3964dcd01749bcc2a29a3089a1c5afcd4d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:34:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] 027 (TKBO): section curve-to-face deviations computed in
 parallel, one projector per worker

IntTools_FaceFace::ComputeTolReached3d measures, for every section curve without a p-curve (section
without approximation, e.g. FreeCAD Part.Shape.section), its largest distance from each face
(FindMaxDistance: about 250 point projections per curve). On a B-spline face each projection runs
Extrema_GenExtPS over the whole face grid, so the step is O(curves x face size): 50-90 % of the
section of the ball screw thread faces.

With theToRunParallel (FreeCAD always sets it) and at least two such curve/face tasks on faces whose
projection runs the grid search (not plane/cylinder/cone/sphere/torus/extrusion/revolution), the tasks
run on OSD_Parallel workers. Each worker owns GeomAPI_ProjectPointOnSurf objects initialised exactly
as IntTools_Context::ProjPS initialises the shared one (BRep_Tool::Surface, the context's UV bounds,
the context tolerance, MIN flag, gradient algorithm), so every value equals the sequential one. The
values are applied in the stock order; max() is exact. A failed task is recomputed by the stock call
in place, so an exception is raised as in stock. Workers: <= logical processors, grids <= ~128 MB.
IntTools_Context gets an inline, non-exported getter of the projection tolerance (no layout change).

INTTOOLS_027_VERIFY: every parallel value compared bit for bit with the stock sequential call;
INTTOOLS_027_MUTANT_B=<factor>: parallel values scaled (negative control of the verify build).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
